{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>Speckled.</b> Mottled with thin patches like dots; פיונטור\"א בְּלַעַ\"ז." "<b>And streaked.</b> A term of טְלָאִים — broad patches." "<b>Brown.</b> Dark, resembling red; רו\"ש בְּלַעַ\"ז — a term as in Mishnah שַׁחֲמָתִית, and it is found white, regarding grain." "<b>And it shall be my wage.</b> Those that will be born from now on — speckled and streaked among the goats and dark among the sheep — shall be mine. And those that are there now, separate them and entrust them into the hand of your sons — so that you will not say to me about those born from now, 'These were already there from the start.' And further, so that you will not say to me, 'Through the males that are speckled and streaked the females will give birth to their like from now on.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "the la'az is Old French pionture, 'spotting/marking'", 1 "the la'az is Old French ros, 'reddish'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:20.793470114Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}